# DataSource Pattern

DataSources live under `src/lib/common/ds/definitions/` and register via `src/lib/common/ds/registry.ts`.

## Basic Shape

```typescript
import type { DataSource } from "@/lib/common/ds/types";
import { DefaultAttribute, DefaultDataSource, DefaultFullAccess } from "@/lib/common/ds/defaults";
import type { Entity } from "@/lib/common/ds/types/module/Entity";

export const EntityDataSource: DataSource = {
  ...DefaultDataSource,
  id: "Entity",
  tableName: "entity",
  attributes: [
    {
      ...DefaultAttribute,
      code: "id",
      name: "ID",
      type: "UUID",
      column: "id",
      primary: true,
      optional: false,
    },
    {
      ...DefaultAttribute,
      code: "name",
      name: "Name",
      type: "Text",
      column: "name",
      maxLength: 120,
      optional: false,
    },
  ],
  access: [{ ...DefaultFullAccess, roleCode: "admin" }],
};
```

## Checklist

1. Add TypeScript type in `src/lib/common/ds/types/...`
2. Add DS definition file
3. Register in module index + `registry.ts`
4. Create page `hooks/use-store.ts` pointing at `datasourceId`

## Attribute Types

`Text` | `Number` | `Boolean` | `Date` | `DateTime` | `UUID` | `JSON`

Keep attribute `code` (camelCase) in sync with the entity interface. Column names are snake_case in SQL.
